flickos-layouts (1.11) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The panel, notifications and the dock run under a supervisor
    (flickos-layout supervise), which restarts one that fails with a
    growing delay and gives up after five failures in a row, and leaves
    alone one that was stopped on purpose or outlived the compositor.
    autostart starts the panel once, so before this a waybar that exited
    (an output changing under it, common in the first seconds of a
    session) left the session without a panel for good.
  * What the panel, the dock and notifications print, and every restart,
    goes to $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/flickos/panel.log: the session's stderr is
    nowhere a user can read, so a failed panel left no trace.
  * Waiting for layout.lock gives up after 10 seconds and carries on
    without it. autostart starts wallpaper, panel, first-run and the
    tiler at once, and one of them hanging while holding the lock must
    not cost the panel.

 -- Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:04:22 +0800

